{"parentUuid":"543ca386-dc7e-4925-82ca-1bbbd3f543db","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_016VRh8xDg8vjLGHx6P8BgSD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01THG7gcDchWnWppsA8myYG6","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"SAT Competition 2025 results CaDiCaL Kissat benchmarks"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20920,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":254,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":20920},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":254,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20920,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":20920,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoorKzg1fXbPkB1Drpx7","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"02e4d3bd-6a5a-4da9-bd4b-21b30f881c06","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:04:51.991Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"740f3b0f-18cd-43c9-9856-b18110858df2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hcrh3wsos2roHTnDqSCkcu","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CaDiCaL SAT solver Learner API export learned clauses\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cadical_sys - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/cadical-sys\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solvers’ API (pysat.solvers) — PySAT 1.9.dev2 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/solvers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Available CAV Evaluation Artifact Reusable CAV Evaluation Artifact CaDiCaL 2.0\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-CAV24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - arminbiere/cadical: CaDiCaL SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - amazon-science/cadical: CaDiCaL SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/amazon-science/cadical\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-65627-9_7\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - jix/pydical: Python wrapper for the CaDiCaL SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jix/pydical\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/src/cadical.hpp at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/src/cadical.hpp\"},{\"title\":\"Deep Integration of SAT Solving and Model Checking\",\"url\":\"https://epub.jku.at/obvulihs/download/pdf/12426345\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL Simplified Satisfiability Solver\",\"url\":\"https://fmv.jku.at/cadical/\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found comprehensive information about the CaDiCaL SAT solver's Learner API for exporting learned clauses:\n\n## CaDiCaL Learner API for Exporting Learned Clauses\n\nThe dynamic API of CaDiCaL interacts and controls the solver during search, and the solver provides dynamic access to clauses learned during conflict analysis to connected Learner instances.\n\n### How the Learner API Works\n\nConnected learners can be used to export learned clauses. The 'learning' function can check the size of the learned clause, and only if it returns true then the individual literals of the learned clause are given to the learn function one by one, terminated by a zero literal.\n\n### State Export Features\n\nIn addition to the dynamic Learner API, CaDiCaL also supports exporting learned clauses through file-based operations. Users can write learned clauses to a file at the end of the solver run using the `--lc-out` command-line argument. Similarly, learned clauses can be read from a file at startup using the `--lc-in` argument.\n\n### Documentation\n\nThe header file of the CaDiCaL library is `src/cadical.hpp` and includes examples for API usage. For more detailed information about implementing the Learner API, you may want to consult the official CaDiCaL repository or documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"89bc9893-eefb-408b-8995-e9de56f317b5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:04:57.481Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"740f3b0f-18cd-43c9-9856-b18110858df2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"02e4d3bd-6a5a-4da9-bd4b-21b30f881c06","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01THG7gcDchWnWppsA8myYG6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT Competition 2025 results CaDiCaL Kissat benchmarks\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Results of SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL, Gimsatul, IsaSAT and Kissat Entering the SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2025-solvers.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Split-BDD Multiplier Verification Benchmarks Submitted to ...\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereKonradKaufmannScholl-SAT-Competition-2025-benchmarks.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - arminbiere/kissat · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat\"},{\"title\":\"Automatically discovering heuristics in a complex SAT ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.22876\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2020 - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0004370221001235\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competitions\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol341-sat2025/html/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27.html\"},{\"title\":\"Proceedings of SAT COMPETITION 2025 Solver and Benchmark Descriptions\",\"url\":\"https://repositum.tuwien.at/bitstream/20.500.12708/218424/2/Codel-2025-Proceedings%20of%20SAT%20Competition%202025%20%20Solver%20and%20Benchmark%20Desc...-vor.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the key findings about the SAT Competition 2025 results for CaDiCaL and Kissat:\n\n## Main Sequential Track UNSAT Results\n\nIn the Main Sequential Track UNSAT category, CaDiCaL-SC2025 achieved first place with a PAR-2 score of 2327.00 and solved 161 instances, followed by Kissat-VSA in second place with a PAR-2 score of 2335.54 and 160 solved instances, and AE-Kissat-bump in third place with a PAR-2 score of 2358.10 and 159 solved instances.\n\n## Memory Infrastructure Challenges\n\nDuring the competition, there were significant memory issues on the new LMU infrastructure, which only had 30 GB of memory compared to the 128 GB developers were accustomed to on StarExec, and several runs crashed at 20 GB allocation due to parsing and proof checking issues on large instances.\n\n## Solver Development Context\n\nPreliminary results suggest that CaDiCaL improvements increase run-time of stand-alone solving substantially and allow solving benchmarks which require bounded variable addition or congruence closures, though it still falls behind Kissat unless proof checking is taken into account, where the combined time of proof production and checking for CaDiCaL is much smaller than for Kissat.\n\nThe complete results and detailed benchmarks for SAT Competition 2025 are available in the official proceedings and results presentations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"148ca66d-6d30-45a7-8c71-2be1cb804e7d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:04:59.295Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"02e4d3bd-6a5a-4da9-bd4b-21b30f881c06","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"543ca386-dc7e-4925-82ca-1bbbd3f543db","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XK9Ub34Gc5kcGReDZMjUTd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CaDiCaL IPASIR-UP interface incremental SAT solving\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL Katalin Fazekas # TU Wien, Austria\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/NEWS.md at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/NEWS.md\"},{\"title\":\"Incremental Inprocessing in SAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://abs.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/2019/FBS_2019.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL(T ): CaDiCaL as CDCL(T ) Engine in cvc5\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~preiner/talks/Preiner-Shonan23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8\"},{\"title\":\"Certifying Incremental SAT Solving Katalin Fazekas 1, Florian Pollitt\",\"url\":\"https://kfazekas.github.io/papers/FazekasPollittFleuryBiere-LPAR24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL A CaDiCaL Integration into CDCL(T )\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/talks/Niemetz-CENTAUR23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Certifying Incremental SAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/FazekasPollittFleuryBiere-LPAR24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"rustsat::solvers - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/rustsat/latest/rustsat/solvers/index.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CaDiCaL IPASIR-UP interface for incremental SAT solving:\n\n## Overview\n\nIPASIR-UP is a general interface designed to inspect and influence the internal behavior of CDCL SAT solvers, capturing essential functionalities that simplify use cases requiring more fine-grained interaction with the SAT solver than provided via the standard IPASIR interface.\n\n## CaDiCaL Integration\n\nThe state-of-the-art SAT solver CaDiCaL was extended with the IPASIR-UP interface and evaluated on two representative use cases: enumerating graphs within the SAT modulo Symmetries framework (SMS), and as the main CDCL(T) SAT engine of the SMT solver cvc5.\n\n## Key Features\n\nCaDiCaL integrates with IPASIR-UP by utilizing notifications like notify_assignment to construct the current partial assignment for observed theory literals, notify_new_decision_level and notify_backtrack to manage incremental solver state, and callbacks like cb_propagate and cb_add_reason_clause_lit for theory propagations and explanations.\n\n## Advantages\n\nUsing CaDiCaL with a SAT solver that implements IPASIR-UP enables easily switching the solver with any other solver implementing the interface, with the advantage that interaction with the SAT layer is standardized and clean without \"hacks\" that may impact performance.\n\n## Performance Note\n\nCaDiCaL with IPASIR-UP shows potential to solve problems outside other solvers' reach.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"68397c89-f70d-4d47-9ba0-1a7371ebf8dd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:04:59.648Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"543ca386-dc7e-4925-82ca-1bbbd3f543db","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
