{"parentUuid":"d4381637-2683-41ad-95dc-bfa858cc22ed","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0154uNUxrwrSeCRRDKWex8uE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016piFEWtfq7PN81MumgegmN","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CaDiCaL industrial application large scale constraint solving case study"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1289,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2744,"cache_read_input_tokens":20920,"output_tokens":500,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2744},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1289,"output_tokens":500,"cache_read_input_tokens":20920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2744,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2744,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoosHJUJEMtjFQqqwATB","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"8d266f07-d8a6-401f-b2ad-aadae00af540","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:07.741Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1e1a1b6a-fb8c-425f-8c29-6957fbed5580","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JZCWpc3zi87mYnZshGZfEd","type":"tool_result","content":"# Learner Class API Analysis\n\nBased on the provided CaDiCaL header file excerpt, the `Learner` class is declared as a forward reference but **not fully documented in the visible content**:\n\n```cpp\nclass Learner;\n```\n\nThe header shows only that a `Learner` callback can be connected via:\n\n```cpp\nvoid connect_learner (Learner *learner);\nvoid disconnect_learner ();\n```\n\n## What's Documented\n\nThe header states this allows \"to export learned clauses\" but provides no method signatures, parameter details, or implementation guidance for the `Learner` interface itself.\n\n## Information Not Available in This Excerpt\n\nThe provided page content does not contain:\n- Method definitions for `Learner` (e.g., `learning()`, `learn()`)\n- Details on clause filtering by size\n- Batch import or reservation APIs\n- Whether all learned clauses are exported or only filtered subsets\n\n**To find this information**, you would need to examine the full `tracer.hpp` or other header files in the CaDiCaL repository that define the complete `Learner` interface implementation."}]},"uuid":"72dba304-c2ea-4a22-9d86-8d367160ab6d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:11.158Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1e1a1b6a-fb8c-425f-8c29-6957fbed5580","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"bf029c0e-2246-441c-a7ad-5c335fc8cd8a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ARzavpNgDgSzy73ud3F5Lk","type":"tool_result","content":"# CaDiCaL Clause Persistence Features\n\nBased on the NEWS.md file, I found **no evidence** of dedicated clause export/import functionality, `--lc-out`, or `--lc-in` options in CaDiCaL.\n\n## Related Features Found\n\n**IPASIR-UP External Propagation** (Version 1.6.0+)\nThe solver introduced \"user propagators for CDCL\" supporting \"external propagation, external decisions, and clause addition during solving.\" This enables dynamic clause insertion but not persistent disk storage.\n\n**Proof Tracing** (Versions 1.7.0+)\nCaDiCaL supports exporting proofs in multiple formats (DRAT, LRAT, FRAT, VeriPB), which document the solving process but differ from learned clause persistence.\n\n**Incremental Lazy Backtracking (ILB)** (Version 1.7.3+)\nAllows \"adding new clauses incrementally while keeping assignments on the trail,\" but again, no disk persistence mechanism is mentioned.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe documentation does not indicate support for learned clause export/import to disk or command-line options for clause persistence across solver invocations. The focus remains on real-time external propagation and proof generation rather than clause database serialization."}]},"uuid":"e3c08289-103d-4363-8fb5-9f225db38b8a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:13.535Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bf029c0e-2246-441c-a7ad-5c335fc8cd8a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d4381637-2683-41ad-95dc-bfa858cc22ed","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LvEoZurCNm7id1ecnSMCob","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"pysat python CaDiCaL Learner callback learned clause export\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SAT solvers’ API (pysat.solvers) — PySAT 1.9.dev2 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/solvers.html\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT Documentation Release 1.9.dev2\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/pysat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT: SAT technology in Python - Usage\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/usage/\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy pysat interface (cpmpy.solvers.pysat) — CPMpy 0.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/min_max_bug/api/solvers/pysat.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - pysathq/pysat: A toolkit for SAT-based prototyping in Python · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pysathq/pysat\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - jix/pydical: Python wrapper for the CaDiCaL SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jix/pydical\"},{\"title\":\"pysat/pysat/solvers.py at master · pysathq/pysat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pysathq/pysat/blob/master/pysat/solvers.py\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy pysat interface (cpmpy.solvers.pysat) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/ufunc/api/solvers/pysat.html\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT: SAT technology in Python - Updates\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/updates/\"},{\"title\":\"Available CAV Evaluation Artifact Reusable CAV Evaluation Artifact CaDiCaL 2.0\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-CAV24.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the relationship between PySAT, Python, CaDiCaL, learner callbacks, and learned clause export:\n\n## PySAT and CaDiCaL Integration\n\nCurrently, the only SAT solver available in PySAT supporting the IPASIR-UP interface is CaDiCaL 1.9.5, which enables advanced features like external propagators and learner callbacks.\n\n## Learner Callbacks and Learned Clauses\n\nThe solver provides dynamic access to clauses learned during conflict analysis to connected Learner instances. This functionality is part of CaDiCaL's dynamic API that allows users to interact with the solver during search.\n\n## Implementation Details\n\nThe method is called by the solver to add an external clause if there is any. The clause can be arbitrary but if it is root-satisfied or tautological, the solver will ignore it without learning it. Root-falsified literals are eagerly removed from the clause.\n\nThe PySAT toolkit provides an interface to CaDiCaL's preprocessor as well as external user-defined engines following the IPASIR-UP interface, which allows for sophisticated manipulation of learned clauses and external reasoning integration.\n\nFor more detailed implementation examples, the documentation recommends examining the source code of BooleanEngine in the PySAT project to see how external reasoning engines can be implemented and attached to CaDiCaL 1.9.5.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e3198ede-799b-419b-b4e7-11124f4c76f3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:15.060Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d4381637-2683-41ad-95dc-bfa858cc22ed","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8d266f07-d8a6-401f-b2ad-aadae00af540","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016piFEWtfq7PN81MumgegmN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CaDiCaL industrial application large scale constraint solving case study\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Constraint Solving at Scale: Optimizing Performance in Complex Parametric Assemblies | International Journal of Emerging Trends in Computer Science and Information Technology\",\"url\":\"https://ijetcsit.org/index.php/ijetcsit/article/view/334/\"},{\"title\":\"Industrial-size job shop scheduling with constraint programming - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2214716022000215\"},{\"title\":\"Solving large scale industrial production scheduling problems with complex constraints: an overview of the state-of-the-art - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1877050922023791\"},{\"title\":\"Building Industrial Applications with Constraint Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/3-540-45406-3_6\"},{\"title\":\"A Constrained Programming Model for the Optimization of Industrial-Scale Scheduling Problems in the Shipbuilding Industry\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2077-1312/11/8/1517\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Programming Based Algorithm for Solving Large-Scale Vehicle Routing Problems | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-29859-3_45\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - NeoCogi/constraint-solver: A generic constraint solver for CAD SW and Simulators · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/NeoCogi/constraint-solver\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Logic Programming for Real-World Test Laboratory Scheduling\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.aaai.org/ojs/16789/16789-13-20283-1-2-20210518.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ConstraintLLM: A Neuro-Symbolic Framework for Industrial ...\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.809.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Constraint Logic Programming\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225597035_Constraint_Logic_Programming\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found information about constraint solving at industrial scale, though the results don't contain specific information about CaDiCaL (a SAT solver) in industrial applications. Here's what I found:\n\n## Industrial-Scale Constraint Solving\n\nDevelopments during the last decade improved the performance of state-of-the-art constraint solvers dramatically, to the point that they can be applied to large-scale instances.\n\nThe rise of Industry 4.0 has led to a significant increase in data collection activities and the gathered information is used to build larger and more complex models. Industrial use cases may consist of several thousand operations on a large variety of machines.\n\n### Key Application Areas\n\nThe performance of state-of-the-art constraint solvers with respect to industrial-size job shop scheduling problem instances has been a focus of analysis, comparing cutting-edge constraint solvers like OR-Tools.\n\nA constrained programming model has been presented for solving an industrial-size instance of the flexible job-shop problem with assemblies and limited buffer capacity based on a real case from the shipbuilding industry.\n\n### Approaches for Large-Scale Problems\n\nAdvanced solution approaches for large scale scheduling problems usually belong to one out of three categories, namely metaheuristic methods, constraint programming and machine learning.\n\nHowever, I did not find specific case studies about CaDiCaL in the search results. CaDiCaL is primarily a SAT solver rather than a general constraint programming solver, so it may be used in different contexts than the industrial constraint programming applications described here.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4f9d6095-8e5a-4619-b2ae-fcae1f251d91","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:15.079Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8d266f07-d8a6-401f-b2ad-aadae00af540","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4f9d6095-8e5a-4619-b2ae-fcae1f251d91","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GJGUwFgZTShBwwSRjj3hGV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FgFdTVim8qYutna5GpZ3se","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arminbiere/cadical/master/src/cadical.hpp","prompt":"Find the Learner class definition. What virtual methods does it expose? Specifically look for: learning(int size), learn(int lit), learn_clause, learning_clause, or similar. Does the Learner only see clauses up to a certain size limit (e.g. tracked via opts like 'shareglue' or 'sharemax')? Also find what add_clause, reserve, freeze, melt do."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5160,"cache_read_input_tokens":23664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5160,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":53,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaootRHUFkQojYxLSuFh1","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"39b3c0bf-9215-4c36-93be-bf6177750a86","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:21.150Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"39b3c0bf-9215-4c36-93be-bf6177750a86","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FgFdTVim8qYutna5GpZ3se","type":"tool_result","content":"# Learner Class Analysis\n\n## Virtual Methods\n\nThe `Learner` class exposes two virtual methods:\n\n1. **`learning(int size)`** - Returns a boolean to check if the solver should export a learned clause of a given size\n2. **`learn(int lit)`** - Receives individual literals of the learned clause, terminated by a zero literal\n\nAs documented: \"The 'learning' can check the size of the learn clause and only if it returns true then the individual literals of the learned clause are given to the learn through 'learn' one by one terminated by a zero literal.\"\n\n## Size Filtering\n\nThe header does not explicitly mention size limits controlled by options like 'shareglue' or 'sharemax'. However, the `learning(int size)` parameter design allows the **connected learner itself to decide** whether to accept clauses based on their size before receiving individual literals.\n\n## Other Methods Clarification\n\n**`freeze()` and `melt()`** are reference-counting methods on the `Solver` class (not `Learner`). They prevent variable elimination by freezing variables across `solve()` calls. Users must freeze variables they plan to reuse incrementally.\n\n**`add()` and related clause methods** (`clause()` overloads) add clauses to the formula itself—these are not learner-related but core solver functionality.\n\nThere is no explicit `add_clause`, `reserve`, or `learning_clause` method in the `Learner` interface shown here."}]},"uuid":"a3888bc7-b1af-41e6-a08b-1c38556bb1e5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:27.426Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"39b3c0bf-9215-4c36-93be-bf6177750a86","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
