{"parentUuid":"4870469b-0e42-4038-a6db-9a90398e83a4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DuYRwwhLC9iaxRQTpzoVb2","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CaDiCaL \"connect_learner\" example C++ API code\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cadical_sys - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/cadical-sys\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - jreeves3/allsat-cadical: all satisfying solutions from CaDiCaL · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jreeves3/allsat-cadical\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - arminbiere/cadical: CaDiCaL SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - jix/pydical: Python wrapper for the CaDiCaL SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jix/pydical\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/releases\"},{\"title\":\"cadical_sys/ lib.rs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/cadical-sys/latest/src/cadical_sys/lib.rs.html\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/README.md at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Incremental usage with API: error vs. solve-status · Issue #2 · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/issues/2\"},{\"title\":\"C++ API Documentation — Bitwuzla documentation\",\"url\":\"https://bitwuzla.github.io/docs/cpp/api.html\"},{\"title\":\"Eagle Mode - C++ API Tutorial - SourceForge\",\"url\":\"https://eaglemode.sourceforge.net/CppApiTutorial.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about CaDiCaL's `connect_learner` functionality:\n\nConnected learners can be used to export learned clauses. The 'learning' can check the size of the learn clause and only if it returns true then the individual literals of the learned clause are given to the learn through 'learn' one by one terminated by a zero literal.\n\nThe header file of the library is src/cadical.hpp and includes an example for API usage. This indicates that the official CaDiCaL repository contains examples and documentation in the header file.\n\nFor a concrete C++ API code example, a simplified C++ example would include the cadical.hpp header and use the CaDiCaL::Solver class to add clauses and call solve().\n\nTo find a specific `connect_learner` example code, you would want to check the official CaDiCaL repository at https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical, particularly the `src/cadical.hpp` header file and the examples directory, which would contain the most up-to-date API documentation and usage examples for this callback mechanism.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"09c9ade2-280f-4f62-94b2-acca087b2ca0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:33.613Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4870469b-0e42-4038-a6db-9a90398e83a4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
