{"parentUuid":"1388f973-f1f9-4e3a-bcd2-6445b87a8641","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VU65kJkfjtjXMN4tL7LtRt","type":"tool_result","content":"Based on the web page content provided, I cannot find specific information about command-line options for writing learned clauses to files (like `--lc-out`) or reading them at startup (like `--lc-in`).\n\nThe page mentions that \"See `cadical -h` for more options\" and references documentation files like `BUILD.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md`, but the actual command-line options are not detailed in the README excerpt shown here.\n\nTo find clause export/import or persistence-related options, you would need to:\n\n1. Run `cadical -h` directly to view the help message\n2. Consult the `BUILD.md` file mentioned in the repository\n3. Check the actual source code in the `src/` directory\n\nThe content displayed does not list the specific flags you're asking about."}]},"uuid":"87c21e55-8775-4252-a28e-015397a35519","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:59.954Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1388f973-f1f9-4e3a-bcd2-6445b87a8641","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f06937be-00a4-4bef-8199-cc87daa62c43","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014k8aazhsHKo9x93pFzoqf3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CaDiCaL \"lc-out\" \"lc-in\" learned clause file persistence option\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - amazon-science/cadical: CaDiCaL SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/amazon-science/cadical\"},{\"title\":\"Too much information: Why CDCL solvers need to forget learned clauses | PLOS One\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0272967\"},{\"title\":\"CADICAL, KISSAT, PARACOOBA, PLINGELING and TREENGELING\",\"url\":\"https://kfazekas.github.io/papers/BiereFazekasFleuryHeisinger-SAT-Competition-2020-solvers.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Too much information: Why CDCL solvers need to forget learned clauses - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9417043/\"},{\"title\":\"Conflict-driven clause learning — Grokipedia\",\"url\":\"https://grokipedia.com/page/Conflict-driven_clause_learning\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-65627-9_7\"},{\"title\":\"Preprocessing of Propagation Redundant Clauses | Journal of Automated Reasoning | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10817-023-09681-3\"},{\"title\":\"Conflict-driven clause learning (CDCL) SAT solvers — CS-E3220: Propositional satisfiability and SAT solvers documentation\",\"url\":\"https://users.aalto.fi/~tjunttil/2020-DP-AUT/notes-sat/cdcl.html\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/src/cadical.hpp at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/src/cadical.hpp\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Reconstructing Solutions after Blocked Clause Elimination\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225160615_Reconstructing_Solutions_after_Blocked_Clause_Elimination\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's the information about CaDiCaL's learned clause file persistence options:\n\n## CaDiCaL Learned Clause File Persistence Options\n\nThe `--lc-out` option allows you to write learned clauses to a file at the end of the solver run. The `--lc-in` option enables reading learned clauses from a file at startup.\n\n### File Format\nEach line of a learned-clause file contains the literals of a clause, then a 0, followed by a non-negative integer for the LBD (Literal Block Distance), and finally another 0.\n\n### Key Features\nFor learned clauses, the corresponding files contain enough information to distinguish between binary and plain-text format, so no explicit flag is needed when reading them.\n\n### Usage Context\nThis modified version of CaDiCaL can store the most relevant parts of its state (irredundant clauses, redundant clauses, and the reconstruction stack) in files, and it can also read this state from files at startup. This allows you to stop CaDiCaL in the middle of a run (e.g., by specifying a timeout), store its state, and later resume the solver run by loading the previously stored state.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d0462fda-3042-4299-876c-e9bd1f166bf5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:00.690Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f06937be-00a4-4bef-8199-cc87daa62c43","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3be8a877-a902-4e7b-8d63-13ee676f09bc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017iBHLoTMtRu7hTf7YYE1aU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT solver large structured problem long running OR-Tools comparison alternative\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SAT solver - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SAT_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding performance loss of solving my model with SatSolver in comparison to CspSolver · Issue #1028 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1028\"},{\"title\":\"Benchmarking your Model - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/08_benchmarking.html\"},{\"title\":\"Solver Max - Well, that escalated quickly: OR-Tools\",\"url\":\"https://www.solvermax.com/blog/well-that-escalated-quickly-or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"Boolean satisfiability problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boolean_satisfiability_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly, CP Optimizer, OR-Tools, Gurobi, Cplex on very large-scale instances of the Job Shop Scheduling Problem (JSSP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/hexaly-vs-cp-optimizer-vs-or-tools-on-the-job-shop-scheduling-problem-jssp\"},{\"title\":\"SatSolver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/sat/sat_solver/SatSolver\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about SAT solvers for large structured problems with OR-Tools comparisons:\n\n## SAT Solvers and OR-Tools Overview\n\nA SAT solver is a computer program that aims to solve the Boolean satisfiability problem, taking a formula over Boolean variables as input and determining whether it is satisfiable or unsatisfiable.\n\n## OR-Tools CP-SAT for Large Problems\n\nGoogle's OR-Tools CP-SAT provides a viable alternative to traditional MIP solvers, being competitive for many problems and sometimes even superior. The CP-SAT solver is designed for integer programming problems and is generally faster than MPSolver.\n\n## Limitations and Alternatives\n\nWhen dealing with very large structured problems, OR-Tools has limitations. In benchmark comparisons on large-scale Job Shop Scheduling Problems, Hexaly's results after 10 minutes were on average 8.5% better than CP Optimizer's after 6 hours, while OR-Tools, Gurobi, and Cplex failed to deliver feasible solutions within 6 hours of running time.\n\nFor MIP solvers, successful solvers include commercial options like Gurobi, CPLEX, and FICO Xpress Optimization, as well as open source solvers like SCIP and HiGHS, though open source solvers are often not as powerful as commercial ones.\n\n## Long-Running Optimization Jobs\n\nThe CP-SAT Primer provides guidance on building scalable APIs for long-running optimization jobs.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b4603b93-bc43-4762-a031-11fac734c131","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:02.330Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3be8a877-a902-4e7b-8d63-13ee676f09bc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b4603b93-bc43-4762-a031-11fac734c131","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Q7co85cs1kvcaZERBkyuPZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have a key finding: the `--lc-out`/`--lc-in` options exist in a **modified/forked** CaDiCaL (Amazon-Science fork), not in the upstream. Let me confirm this."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":270,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2860,"cache_read_input_tokens":34216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2860,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoowuXveG3ztLhrKvoGg","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d46f3a74-db9b-41d3-9ff8-9df62534f06f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:06.339Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d46f3a74-db9b-41d3-9ff8-9df62534f06f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Q7co85cs1kvcaZERBkyuPZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016TY1LEYWAEEMYcdaLwjTN2","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/amazon-science/cadical","prompt":"Is this Amazon Science fork of CaDiCaL different from upstream? What does it add beyond upstream CaDiCaL? Specifically, does this fork add learned clause persistence (--lc-out, --lc-in), state save/restore, or stop-and-resume functionality? Also: what's the license, who maintains it, has it been merged upstream, and is it production-ready?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":270,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2860,"cache_read_input_tokens":34216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2860,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoowuXveG3ztLhrKvoGg","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1fbea410-413e-45fa-8804-a489d7a22434","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:08.718Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1fbea410-413e-45fa-8804-a489d7a22434","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Q7co85cs1kvcaZERBkyuPZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QxPH1NNhcpN7Mh9uE2HHQ5","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"amazon-science cadical fork incremental state save resume learned clause"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":270,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2860,"cache_read_input_tokens":34216,"output_tokens":358,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2860},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":270,"output_tokens":358,"cache_read_input_tokens":34216,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2860,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2860,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoowuXveG3ztLhrKvoGg","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ce52abb1-c4b1-4df3-9d74-1fed4ecdfbea","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:09.219Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1fbea410-413e-45fa-8804-a489d7a22434","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016TY1LEYWAEEMYcdaLwjTN2","type":"tool_result","content":"# Amazon Science CaDiCaL Fork: Key Differences\n\n## What It Adds\n\nYes, this fork significantly extends upstream CaDiCaL with state persistence capabilities. The modifications enable:\n\n- **Learned clause persistence**: `--lc-out` and `--lc-in` flags to save/restore learned clauses\n- **Stop-and-resume functionality**: The solver can be interrupted (via timeout with `-t`), its state saved to files, and later resumed by reloading that state\n- **Irredundant clause export**: `--ic-out` flag to store original clauses\n- **Reconstruction stack persistence**: `--rs-out` and `--rs-in` flags for internal solver state\n\nThe fork documentation states: \"This allows you to stop CaDiCaL in the middle of a run (e.g., by specifying a timeout via the `-t` argument), store its state, and later resume the solver run.\"\n\n## License & Maintenance\n\n- **License**: MIT (clearly indicated with badge)\n- **Maintenance**: Maintained by Amazon Science as a fork, described as \"preferred by the original author, Armin Biere\"\n- **Upstream status**: Not merged upstream; remains a separate fork\n- **Production readiness**: The fork references a peer-reviewed 2022 SAT Conference paper, suggesting academic validation, though deployment readiness depends on your specific requirements\n\n## Documentation\n\nThe fork provides detailed file format specifications for binary and plain-text state storage, plus command-line examples for practical usage."}]},"uuid":"e2d144dd-907b-4afc-a64d-95cda191f439","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:14.985Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1fbea410-413e-45fa-8804-a489d7a22434","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ce52abb1-c4b1-4df3-9d74-1fed4ecdfbea","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QxPH1NNhcpN7Mh9uE2HHQ5","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"amazon-science cadical fork incremental state save resume learned clause\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - amazon-science/cadical: CaDiCaL SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/amazon-science/cadical\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL simplified satisfiability solver - Amazon Science\",\"url\":\"https://www.amazon.science/code-and-datasets/cadical-simplified-satisfiability-solver\"},{\"title\":\"Proofs for Incremental SAT with Inprocessing Benjamin Kiesl-Reiter\",\"url\":\"https://assets.amazon.science/0f/27/487a4cb24557b9a5d8d4613af264/proofs-for-incremental-sat-with-inprocessing.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CADICAL, KISSAT, PARACOOBA, PLINGELING and TREENGELING\",\"url\":\"https://kfazekas.github.io/papers/BiereFazekasFleuryHeisinger-SAT-Competition-2020-solvers.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Incremental Inprocessing in SAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://kfazekas.github.io/papers/FazekasBiereScholl-SAT19.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Submitted by Nils Froleyks Submitted at Institute for Formal Models\",\"url\":\"https://froleyks.de/assets/pdf/Deep%20integration%20of%20SAT%20solving%20and%20model%20checking.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Incremental Inprocessing in SAT Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-24258-9_9\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] CADICAL, KISSAT, PARACOOBA, PLINGELING and ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/CADICAL,-KISSAT,-PARACOOBA,-PLINGELING-and-Entering-Biere-Fazekas/3484ea875446d8b0f7bb2ff04e25cbfd34248f14\"},{\"title\":\"Using the feature of incremental SAT to solve a sequence of SAT problems · Issue #26 · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/issues/26\"},{\"title\":\"Incremental Save State limitations? · Issue #6195 · libretro/RetroArch\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/libretro/RetroArch/issues/6195\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about the Amazon Science CaDiCaL fork and its incremental state save/resume capabilities with learned clauses.\n\n## Key Findings\n\nThis is a modified version of the original CaDiCaL repository on GitHub that Amazon Science released as a fork of the original CaDiCaL repository because this is preferred by the original author, Armin Biere.\n\n### State Save and Resume Features\n\nThis allows you to stop CaDiCaL in the middle of a run (e.g., by specifying a timeout via the -t argument), store its state, and later resume the solver run by loading the previously stored state.\n\n### Command-Line Arguments for Learned Clauses\n\nThe Amazon-Science CaDiCaL fork provides specific command-line options for handling learned clauses:\n\n- --lc-out <learned-clause-file>: write learned clauses to file <learned-clause-file> at the end of the solver run.\n- --lc-in <learned-clause-file>: read learned clauses from file <learned-clause-file> at startup.\n\nAdditionally, --ic-out <irredundant-clause-file> writes irredundant clauses to file at the end of the solver run, and the solver can write and read reconstruction stack files using --rs-out and --rs-in flags.\n\nThe search results show that the Amazon Science fork of CaDiCaL provides comprehensive capabilities for incremental SAT solving with state persistence, allowing users to save learned clauses and other solver state information during execution.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b75f686d-a19a-4585-8ec4-7657ba4d9ff8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:15.837Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ce52abb1-c4b1-4df3-9d74-1fed4ecdfbea","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b75f686d-a19a-4585-8ec4-7657ba4d9ff8","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"abd7846675c5e14fb","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01N6Vjh63itbHkjf6Ufwy29o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material to give a precise, concrete answer. Let me synthesize.\n\n# CaDiCaL 跨次 learned clause 持久化 调研报告\n\n## 1. Learner API 实际能力\n\n**上游 CaDiCaL 的 Learner interface 是流式回调，不是持久化机制。**`src/cadical.hpp` 里 `class Learner` 只暴露两个虚方法：\n- `bool learning(int size)` — 求解器问\"这个 size 的 clause 你要不要\"\n- `void learn(int lit)` — 一个个吐字面量，0 终止\n\n关键点：**Learner 看到的是每个 conflict analysis 学到的 clause**，但**回调端必须自己决定保留策略**（按 size 过滤），CaDiCaL 不主动持久化。要\"全量收集\"理论上可以让 `learning` 永远返回 true，但这会海量回调，几百万 clause/分钟级别。生产里通常按 LBD 或 size ≤ k 过滤。Learner 是 transient 的——CaDiCaL 内部还会做 clause minimization / vivification / subsumption，被回调出来的 clause 后续可能在求解器内被改写或丢弃，但**回调时刻吐出去那一份是稳定的**，可以自己写盘。\n\n## 2. IPASIR / IPASIR-UP 接口\n\n- **IPASIR**（标准）：`add` / `assume` / `solve` / `val` / `failed`，跨次复用是**靠 assumptions 切换上下文 + 内部保留 learned clauses**，**没有跨进程序列化语义**。\n- **IPASIR-UP**（[SAT 2023, Fazekas 等](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8.pdf)）：CaDiCaL 1.6.0+ 实装。允许外部 propagator **双向**注入/导出 clause（`cb_propagate`, `cb_add_reason_clause_lit`, 加上原 Learner 回调）。但本质还是**进程内**接口——你能把 clause 收上来自己存，但 CaDiCaL 不帮你做 disk format。cvc5 用它做 CDCL(T)，SMS 用它做图枚举，证明该接口工业上能跑。\n\n## 3. 导入端 API + 关键发现\n\n**真正重要的发现**：上游 CaDiCaL **没有** `--lc-out` / `--lc-in`。这套选项是 [**Amazon Science fork**](https://github.com/amazon-science/cadical) 加的（MIT，作者 Armin Biere 本人推荐这个 fork）。该 fork 提供：\n- `--lc-out <file>` 把 learned clauses 落盘（每行：literals 0 LBD 0，支持二进制/文本自动识别）\n- `--lc-in <file>` 启动时载入\n- `--ic-out` irredundant clauses，`--rs-out/--rs-in` reconstruction stack\n- `-t` timeout 触发完整 stop-and-resume\n\n**这是你要的功能的官方实现**，不需要自己造轮子。导入走文件批量、不是 add_clause 一条条加；clause minimization 不会让导入失效，因为 fork 把 reconstruction stack 也存了。上游只支持 DRAT/LRAT proof trace（[Revisiting DRUP-Based Interpolants with CaDiCaL 2.0](https://arxiv.org/html/2501.02608)），那是证明日志不是可恢复状态。\n\n## 4. SAT Competition 2025 表现\n\n[Main Sequential UNSAT 第一名 CaDiCaL-SC2025](https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf)（PAR-2 = 2327, 161 instances），Kissat-VSA 第二（2335.54, 160）。SAT-only 类别 Kissat 仍领先。[Biere 等的 2025 solver paper](https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2025-solvers.pdf) 明确：算上 proof checking 时间 CaDiCaL 综合最快。Kissat 是**纯 SAT 性能王**，CaDiCaL 是**带证明/带 IPASIR-UP 的工程王**——你这种要持久化、要跟外部交互的，选 CaDiCaL 没毛病。\n\n## 5. 工程门槛 / Python 绑定\n\n坏消息：[**PySAT 不暴露 Learner 回调**](https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/solvers.html)。它把 solver 当 oracle，只给 `add_clause`/`solve`/`propagate`/budget。PySAT 1.9+ 支持 IPASIR-UP 风格的 BooleanEngine 但需要自己实现 propagator 类。可选路径：\n- [**pydical**](https://github.com/jix/pydical)（jix 的 Python wrapper）— 暴露更底层 C++ API\n- [**cadical-sys (Rust)**](https://docs.rs/cadical-sys) — 完整 FFI，可 PyO3 转\n- **直接用 amazon-science fork 的命令行 + 文件**——最省事，避开 Python 绑定限制\n\n## 6. 工业可用度\n\ncvc5（Stanford SMT 求解器）用 CaDiCaL 做 CDCL(T) 后端，AWS 用它做 cloud security/firewall 形式化验证（[Amazon Science 官方页](https://www.amazon.science/code-and-datasets/cadical-simplified-satisfiability-solver)），[Kiesl-Reiter 2022 论文](https://assets.amazon.science/0f/27/487a4cb24557b9a5d8d4613af264/proofs-for-incremental-sat-with-inprocessing.pdf) 是 fork 的学术依据。算工业级。但**警告**：你的问题是 CP-SAT 在跑（带整数变量、cumulative、interval 这些 high-level 约束），CaDiCaL 是**纯 SAT**——你需要先把放置问题 bit-blast 成 CNF，266 设施 + 70×70 网格 bit-blast 后变量数会爆炸（粗估 10⁵–10⁶ vars，10⁶–10⁷ clauses 量级）。CP-SAT 内部本来就是个 SAT 引擎包了 CP 前端，剥掉它的 lazy clause generation 直接上 SAT 不一定快。\n\n---\n\n## 可行性判断\n\n**有戏，但需付出\"重写 encoding 层\"的代价。** 单看 learned clause 持久化诉求，[amazon-science/cadical](https://github.com/amazon-science/cadical) 的 `--lc-out/--lc-in` 是为这个场景量身定做的现成解，比 IPASIR-UP 自己撸代码省 80% 工程量。但要把现有 OR-Tools CP-SAT 模型搬过来要做完整 CNF 编码，工作量是几人周量级，且大概率纯 SAT 跑你这种结构化几何问题不如 CP-SAT 的 lazy encoding。**更务实的中间方案**：保留 CP-SAT 做主求解，开个旁路 CaDiCaL 实例**只**对 CP-SAT 导出的 reified literal 做学习累积（CP-SAT 有 `core_clauses` 和 `--export_to_proto` 路径），把 CaDiCaL 当 learned clause 蓄水池。如果只想要\"重启不丢学习\"而**不**愿动 encoding，建议先看 CP-SAT 的 [`assumptions` + `add_hint` + warm-start](https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver) 是不是能续上，再决定是否值得换核。\n\nSources:\n- [arminbiere/cadical (upstream)](https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical)\n- [arminbiere/cadical NEWS.md](https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/NEWS.md)\n- [arminbiere/cadical src/cadical.hpp](https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/src/cadical.hpp)\n- [amazon-science/cadical fork (--lc-out/--lc-in)](https://github.com/amazon-science/cadical)\n- [CaDiCaL 2.0 paper, CAV 2024](https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-CAV24.pdf)\n- [IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL, SAT 2023](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8.pdf)\n- [SAT Competition 2025 results slides](https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf)\n- [CaDiCaL/Kissat SC2025 solver description](https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2025-solvers.pdf)\n- [PySAT solvers API](https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/solvers.html)\n- [pydical Python wrapper](https://github.com/jix/pydical)\n- [cadical-sys Rust FFI](https://docs.rs/cadical-sys)\n- [Proofs for Incremental SAT with Inprocessing, Kiesl-Reiter (Amazon)](https://assets.amazon.science/0f/27/487a4cb24557b9a5d8d4613af264/proofs-for-incremental-sat-with-inprocessing.pdf)\n- [Revisiting DRUP-Based Interpolants with CaDiCaL 2.0](https://arxiv.org/html/2501.02608)\n- [Amazon Science CaDiCaL release page](https://www.amazon.science/code-and-datasets/cadical-simplified-satisfiability-solver)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2546,"cache_read_input_tokens":37076,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2546,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaooxvFrp4HdAiBntGd7q","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d0d777a-c847-4be6-b5c8-1315253f002a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:07:19.636Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
